WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.127 --> 00:00:18.670
next day Katie and Joy rode their bicycles to Boone Elementary School.

2
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.211
They were both excited.

3
00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:25.794
Katie couldn't wait for everyone to see her new bangs.

4
00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:29.856
And Joy wanted to tell everyone about the chickens.

5
00:00:33.576 --> 00:00:34.417
"There's Luke!"

6
00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:35.817
shouted Joy.

7
00:00:36.358 --> 00:00:40.240
She waved at a boy in a T-shirt that said "I DIG WORMS."

8
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.441
Luke was Katie and Joy's cousin.

9
00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:48.404
"Joy," said Katie, "why don't you wait until Mr.

10
00:00:48.464 --> 00:00:50.205
Higgins starts the science lesson?

11
00:00:51.226 --> 00:00:53.487
Then tell everybody about the chicks.

12
00:00:54.127 --> 00:00:56.629
Learning about animals is part of science."

13
00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.270
Joy hesitated.

14
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.572
"Well, if you think so," she said.

15
00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:04.865
"I guess I could wait until science."

16
00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:08.286
But Katie didn't wait to share her news.

17
00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:09.946
"Hey, Luke!

18
00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:11.506
I've got bangs!

19
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:14.467
Now nobody will mix me up with Joy!"

20
00:01:14.487 --> 00:01:19.149
"Oh. That's good, I guess," Luke replied.

21
00:01:19.169 --> 00:01:21.869
"How's your bait business?"

22
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.050
asked Katie.

23
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.911
Luke collected earthworms and sold them to fishermen at the gas station.

24
00:01:27.931 --> 00:01:30.792
"Excellent," said Luke.

25
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.961
"On Saturday I sold eight cups of worms for a dollar each.

26
00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:37.422
Wait until summer.

27
00:01:37.942 --> 00:01:39.962
I won't be able to keep up with the demand."

28
00:01:41.503 --> 00:01:42.583
"Here comes Laura!"

29
00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.044
exclaimed Joy.

30
00:01:44.624 --> 00:01:46.944
Laura Layman was in the third grade too.

31
00:01:46.964 --> 00:01:48.965
"What's new?"

32
00:01:49.505 --> 00:01:50.225
Laura asked.

33
00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:54.086
"I've got bangs," Katie blurted out.

34
00:01:54.106 --> 00:01:59.848
"And I've got something exciting to tell everyone," Joy whispered to Laura.

35
00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:02.268
"But I can't say it yet."

36
00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:07.110
Ms. Olson, the school principal, stood outside the front door.

37
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.231
"Good morning, twins," she said.

38
00:02:10.251 --> 00:02:12.731
"Good morning, Luke, Laura."

39
00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:14.512
"Good morning, Ms.

40
00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:16.072
Olson," said Katie.

41
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:20.993
"From now on remember—Katie is the one with bangs."

42
00:02:21.013 --> 00:02:25.375
"Okay. That's nice to know," replied Ms.

43
00:02:25.455 --> 00:02:27.495
Olson. Mr.

44
00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:30.536
Higgins waited by the door to the third-grade classroom.

45
00:02:31.804 --> 00:02:32.524
"Hello, Luke.

46
00:02:33.104 --> 00:02:34.685
Hello, Laura," he said.

47
00:02:34.705 --> 00:02:36.105
"Hello, twins."

48
00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:39.526
"Katie here," stated Katie.

49
00:02:39.546 --> 00:02:41.527
"I'm the one with bangs."

50
00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:46.008
She thought, "It's going to be a great day."

51
00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:50.550
The first activity of the day was a math worksheet.

52
00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.251
Katie got three division problems wrong.

53
00:02:54.851 --> 00:02:56.211
Joy solved them all.

54
00:02:57.332 --> 00:03:02.577
During spelling time Katie spelled "cheese" with a z instead of an s.

55
00:03:03.857 --> 00:03:05.878
Joy spelled every word right.

56
00:03:07.078 --> 00:03:11.280
When it was time for art, Katie's clay horse would not stand up.

57
00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.201
But Joy's clay sheep looked perfect.

58
00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:19.462
"What is happening to my great day?"

59
00:03:19.922 --> 00:03:20.742
wondered Katie.

60
00:03:21.903 --> 00:03:24.343
She had a feeling that things would get worse.

61
00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:30.327
Science was next, and that meant Joy would soon have everyone's attention.

62
00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:35.691
First, Luke showed the class a creepy earthworm he dug up.

63
00:03:36.212 --> 00:03:38.593
It was 23 centimeters long!

64
00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.956
Next, Joy raised her hand.

65
00:03:43.417 --> 00:03:44.899
Katie jumped out of her seat.

66
00:03:44.919 --> 00:03:47.180
"Guess what?"

67
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.342
Mr. Higgins and the class looked at Katie.

68
00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:53.566
"We're getting baby chickens," said Katie.

69
00:03:54.106 --> 00:03:55.687
She heard Joy gasp.

70
00:03:57.548 --> 00:03:59.889
"That's big news," said Mr.

71
00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.051
Higgins. "How old will they be?"

72
00:04:02.071 --> 00:04:07.094
"Um, they'll be really little," Katie said quickly.

73
00:04:07.114 --> 00:04:10.576
"One day old," Joy answered.

74
00:04:11.677 --> 00:04:13.197
Mr. Higgins turned to Joy.

75
00:04:13.217 --> 00:04:15.019
"Oh," he said.

76
00:04:16.219 --> 00:04:17.680
Then he looked back at Katie.

77
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.142
"How many chicks are you getting?"

78
00:04:20.162 --> 00:04:23.964
"Maybe three," replied Katie.

79
00:04:24.508 --> 00:04:27.969
She looked over at Joy, who narrowed her eyes at Katie.

80
00:04:27.989 --> 00:04:31.230
"Six," Joy corrected her.

81
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.331
"What do chicks eat?"

82
00:04:33.891 --> 00:04:34.431
asked Mr.

83
00:04:34.451 --> 00:04:37.312
Higgins. "Are you getting a rooster?"

84
00:04:37.852 --> 00:04:38.432
asked Luke.

85
00:04:38.452 --> 00:04:41.073
"Will they miss their mother?"

86
00:04:41.093 --> 00:04:42.333
asked Laura.

87
00:04:43.573 --> 00:04:46.474
Katie was sorry that she had opened her big mouth.

88
00:04:47.034 --> 00:04:48.915
She had ruined things for Joy.

89
00:04:50.115 --> 00:04:52.656
And now she couldn't answer a single question.

90
00:04:53.264 --> 00:04:54.665
She looked over at Joy.

91
00:04:54.685 --> 00:05:01.049
"Well," Joy said, taking over, "first, they will have special feed."

92
00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:07.253
She pulled out her chicken catalog, and everyone gathered around Joy's desk.

93
00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:12.517
"Here are the kinds of chickens we picked out," she explained proudly.

94
00:05:13.617 --> 00:05:16.920
Katie stayed at her desk, listening in silence.
